IMPORT prelude

-- Hotels Act 1954 (Singapore) -- what counts as a hotel (s 2) and the presumption in a prosecution (s 14), registration of
-- premises (ss 5, 6), the manager's licence and its calendar-year life (s 7), suspension, cancellation and when it takes effect
-- (ss 8, 9), appeal to the Minister (s 11), exemption (s 12), the licensee's liability for staff (s 13), entry and inspection
-- (s 15), and the offences and penalties (s 16).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HA1954.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- retrieval record calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026. No later amendment is annotated in the text; the last
-- amending Act in the legislative history is Act 7 of 1996 (Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act 1996). The section
-- numbers follow the BODY: the arrangement at the top of the deposit is out of step by one (it lists "Short title" against 2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0061 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (17 sections), so nearly all of it that bears on a hotel operator, an owner or a guest is here.
-- Not encoded: the constitution of the Board and its officers (ss 3, 4), reclassification beyond noting it is not appealable
-- (s 10), the regulation-making power (s 17), and anything in the regulations themselves (fees, forms, classes, prescribed
-- licence conditions, exemptions), none of which was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hotels Act 1954 -- hotels`

§§ `2, 12 -- what is a hotel`

-- s 2: "hotel" includes "a boarding house, lodging house, guesthouse and any building or premises not being a public institution
-- and containing not less than 4 rooms or cubicles in which persons are harboured or lodged for hire or reward of any kind and
-- where any domestic service is provided by the owner, lessee, tenant, occupier or manager for the person so harboured or lodged".
-- READING (an inference, not settled by the text): the named kinds (boarding house, lodging house, guesthouse) are hotels in their
-- own right, and the 4-room, hire and domestic-service qualifiers attach only to "any building or premises".
-- s 12: the Act does "not apply to any premises or class of premises exempted by regulations made under this Act".
DECLARE Premises HAS
    `is a boarding house, lodging house or guesthouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a public institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rooms or cubicles` IS A NUMBER
    `persons lodged for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `domestic service provided to them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shortest letting period in days` IS A NUMBER
    `exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are a hotel` IF
        `the premises`'s `is a boarding house, lodging house or guesthouse`
    OR  (     (NOT `the premises`'s `is a public institution`)
          AND `the premises`'s `rooms or cubicles` AT LEAST 4
          AND `the premises`'s `persons lodged for hire or reward`
          AND `the premises`'s `domestic service provided to them`)

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the premises` IF
    `the premises are a hotel` `the premises` AND (NOT `the premises`'s `exempted by regulations`)

§§ `14 -- the presumption in a prosecution`

-- s 14: "In any prosecution under this Act, it shall be presumed until the contrary is proved -- (a) that any premises in which
-- rooms or parts of rooms are let or sublet for hire for periods of less than one week constitute a hotel".
-- The presumption names no room count and no domestic service. A two-room flat let by the night is presumed a hotel until the
-- defence proves otherwise.
GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court treats the premises as a hotel` IF
        `the premises are a hotel` `the premises`
    OR  (     `the premises`'s `shortest letting period in days` < 7
          AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`))

§§ `5, 6 -- registration of premises`

-- s 5(1): "No premises shall be used as a hotel unless they are registered". (2) application to the Board in the prescribed form;
-- (3) the Board "may", after inquiry and "on payment of the prescribed fee", grant a certificate; (4) the Board "may, in its
-- discretion, refuse to register any premises as a hotel without assigning any reason therefor".
-- s 6: no certificate unless the Board is satisfied (a) not to be conducted as a disorderly house; (b) structurally adapted; (c)
-- proper provision for sanitation; (d) situation suitable; (e) standard of accommodation adequate for the class applied for.
DECLARE RegistrationApplication HAS
    `made in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed fee paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `will not be a disorderly house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `structurally adapted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proper sanitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `situation suitable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accommodation adequate for the class sought` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A RegistrationApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may register the premises` IF
        `the application`'s `made in the prescribed form`
    AND `the application`'s `prescribed fee paid`
    AND `the application`'s `will not be a disorderly house`
    AND `the application`'s `structurally adapted`
    AND `the application`'s `proper sanitation`
    AND `the application`'s `situation suitable`
    AND `the application`'s `accommodation adequate for the class sought`

-- Nothing in ss 5 or 6 ever obliges the Board to register: s 5(4) lets it refuse without reasons even when s 6 is met.
GIVEN `the application` IS A RegistrationApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is entitled to registration` IF FALSE

§§ `7 -- the manager's licence`

-- s 7(1): no person shall keep or manage premises for the purposes of a hotel "unless he is the holder of a valid licence granted
-- in respect of the premises". (2) granted "on payment of the prescribed fees". (6) no licence unless the applicant satisfies the
-- Board that (a) the premises will not be conducted as a disorderly house and (b) "he is of good character and a fit and proper
-- person". (7) the Board may refuse to grant or renew "without assigning any reason therefor".
DECLARE LicenceApplication HAS
    `prescribed fees paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `premises will not be a disorderly house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of good character and fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A LicenceApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may grant the licence` IF
        `the application`'s `prescribed fees paid`
    AND `the application`'s `premises will not be a disorderly house`
    AND `the application`'s `of good character and fit and proper`

-- s 7(5)(b): every licence is "granted on or after 1 January in every year and shall expire on 31 December next following the date
-- of grant". A licence granted in mid-December runs for a fortnight.
GIVEN `grant year` IS A NUMBER, `year asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence is current in that year` IF
    `year asked about` EQUALS `grant year`

GIVEN `day of the year granted` IS A NUMBER, `days in that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the days the licence runs` IS
    `days in that year` - `day of the year granted` + 1

§§ `8, 9 -- suspension and cancellation`

-- s 8(2): for an "unclean or insanitary condition" the Board may by written notice require the hotel-keeper to remedy the defect
-- "within such period not being less than one month as may be specified". (3) if the defect is not remedied within the period,
-- the Board may suspend or cancel the certificate and cancel the licence.
GIVEN `period specified in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remedy period is lawful` IF
    `period specified in months` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `written notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `period specified in months` IS A NUMBER, `period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `defect remedied to the Board's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may suspend or cancel for insanitary condition` IF
        `written notice given`
    AND `the remedy period is lawful` `period specified in months`
    AND `period has expired`
    AND (NOT `defect remedied to the Board's satisfaction`)

-- s 8(4): no suspension or cancellation under (1) or (3) "shall take effect until the expiration of 10 days from the date of the
-- suspension or cancellation". (5) where an appeal is made within the 10 days of s 11, it "shall not take effect until the appeal
-- has been determined and the Minister confirms the suspension or cancellation".
-- INFERENCE: the 10 days are counted excluding the day of the decision, so the decision takes effect once more than 10 days have
-- passed. The cases avoid the boundary day.
GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER, `appealed within 10 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal determined` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 8 suspension or cancellation has taken effect` IF
        `days since the decision` > 10
    AND (    (NOT `appealed within 10 days`)
          OR (`appeal determined` AND `Minister confirmed`))

-- s 9: where a hotel-keeper "is convicted of an offence under Part 11 of the Women's Charter 1961, the Board SHALL" cancel the
-- licence and the certificate of the hotel where the offence was committed. No discretion, and no appeal under s 11.
GIVEN `convicted under Part 11 of the Women's Charter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must cancel licence and registration` IF
    `convicted under Part 11 of the Women's Charter`

§§ `10, 11 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 11: a person aggrieved by (a) refusal to register; (b) refusal to grant or renew a licence; (c) suspension or cancellation of a
-- certificate "under section 8"; or (d) cancellation of a licence "under section 8" may, "within 10 days from the date of the
-- refusal, suspension or cancellation, appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be final and conclusive".
-- Not listed: mandatory cancellation on conviction (s 9), reclassification to a lower class (s 10), and a court's cancellation
-- under s 16(8).
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal to register premises`
    `refusal to grant or renew a licence`
    `section 8 suspension or cancellation of registration`
    `section 8 cancellation of a licence`
    `section 9 cancellation on conviction`
    `reclassification to a lower class`
    `cancellation by a court on conviction`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is appealable` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal to register premises` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusal to grant or renew a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 8 suspension or cancellation of registration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 8 cancellation of a licence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister is in time` IF
    `the decision is appealable` `the decision` AND `days since the decision` AT MOST 10

§§ `13 -- the licensee answers for staff`

-- s 13(1): a licensee liable to a pecuniary penalty or forfeiture for an act or default "shall be liable to the same pecuniary
-- penalty or forfeiture for every similar act ... of any agent or servant employed by him in the course of his business".
-- (2): "Every person who appears to be employed in any hotel registered under this Act" is deemed the licensee's servant.
-- (3): the agent or servant remains liable.
GIVEN `the act would make the licensee liable if his own` IS A BOOLEAN, `done by an agent or servant in the course of the business` IS A BOOLEAN, `doer appears to be employed in the registered hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee is liable for the act` IF
        `the act would make the licensee liable if his own`
    AND (`done by an agent or servant in the course of the business` OR `doer appears to be employed in the registered hotel`)

§§ `15 -- entry and inspection`

-- s 15(1): the chairman, any member of the Board, "or any person duly authorised by the chairman in writing" may "at any time of
-- the day or night without previous notice enter and inspect any hotel or any premises reasonably suspected of being used for the
-- purposes of a hotel". (2) refusing or obstructing entry or inspection is an offence.
DECLARE Inspector IS ONE OF
    `the chairman of the Board`
    `a member of the Board`
    `a person authorised by the chairman in writing`
    `a person authorised by the chairman orally`
    `the secretary of the Board without written authority`

GIVEN `the inspector` IS AN Inspector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inspector has the power of entry` IF
    CONSIDER `the inspector`
    WHEN `the chairman of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person authorised by the chairman in writing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Time of day and notice do not enter the test at all; they are parameters only so the cases can say so.
GIVEN `the inspector` IS AN Inspector, `place is a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN, `place reasonably suspected of hotel use` IS A BOOLEAN, `at night` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is lawful` IF
    `the inspector has the power of entry` `the inspector` AND (`place is a hotel` OR `place reasonably suspected of hotel use`)

§§ `16 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 16: (1) keeping or managing premises as a hotel with no certificate of registration in force; (2) as owner or occupier,
-- permitting unregistered premises to be used as a hotel; (3) keeping or managing a hotel without a valid licence; (4) as owner or
-- occupier, permitting an unlicensed person to manage or keep the premises as a hotel; (5) a hotel-keeper contravening a condition
-- of his licence; (6) for the grant or renewal of a certificate or licence, making a declaration or statement "false in any
-- material particular or knowingly" uttering, producing or using one; s 15(2) refusing or obstructing inspection.
-- On (6): "knowingly" governs only uttering, producing and using. MAKING the false statement carries no knowledge requirement on
-- the words.
-- s 12 is applied to (1) to (4): exempted premises need neither registration nor a licence.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `premises exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `keeps or manages the premises as a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate of registration in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid licence for the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permits the premises to be used as a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permits an unlicensed person to keep or manage them as a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a hotel-keeper contravening a licence condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a materially false statement to obtain a certificate or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used a materially false statement to obtain a certificate or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refused or obstructed an inspection` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping an unregistered hotel` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `premises exempted by regulations`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `keeps or manages the premises as a hotel`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `certificate of registration in force`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permitting an unregistered hotel` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `premises exempted by regulations`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `is the owner or occupier`
    AND `the conduct`'s `permits the premises to be used as a hotel`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `certificate of registration in force`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping a hotel without a licence` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `premises exempted by regulations`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `keeps or manages the premises as a hotel`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `holds a valid licence for the premises`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permitting an unlicensed keeper` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `premises exempted by regulations`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `is the owner or occupier`
    AND `the conduct`'s `permits an unlicensed person to keep or manage them as a hotel`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `making or using a false statement` IF
        `the conduct`'s `made a materially false statement to obtain a certificate or licence`
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `used a materially false statement to obtain a certificate or licence` AND `the conduct`'s `knew the statement was false`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under the Act` IF
        `keeping an unregistered hotel` `the conduct`
    OR  `permitting an unregistered hotel` `the conduct`
    OR  `keeping a hotel without a licence` `the conduct`
    OR  `permitting an unlicensed keeper` `the conduct`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is a hotel-keeper contravening a licence condition`
    OR  `making or using a false statement` `the conduct`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `refused or obstructed an inspection`

-- s 16(7): "a fine not exceeding $2,000 and, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, to such fine or to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 6 months or to both". (8) the court may also cancel or suspend the certificate and cancel the licence.
-- A first offence carries no imprisonment at all.
GIVEN `previous convictions under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS 2000

GIVEN `previous convictions under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    IF `previous convictions under the Act` AT LEAST 1 THEN 6 ELSE 0
